/-!
# Restart charts instantiated on retained counterflow and own records

Packet PROVE-AUX61-R1. `exists_history_restart_chart` constructs a measurable
chart from the actual histories, with countable approaches selected in the
recorded own and original-target charts. `exists_measurable_own_inherited_shift`
preserves the exact inherited chain-rule branch, and
`exists_driver_of_history_restart_chart` supplies the fresh compact-slit driver.

The target collar, its prime-end comparison with the current collar, the
history-measurable component selector, and the canonical additional logarithm
remain explicit inputs. No field kernel or unconditional restart theorem is
asserted by these conditional adapters.
